Subject: [PATCH] soundwire: qcom: keep the bus for deferred codec probes

A controller probe running on the deferred-probe worker can wait for codecs
whose GPIO/reset suppliers are queued behind that same probe. The fatal
boot timeout deletes the codecs before their suppliers can bind.

Keep the initialized bus registered so deferred probing can finish. Only
report complete enumeration when all slaves are online. Hardware init and
DAI registration failures still use the existing cleanup paths.

On the A16, the failing trace deletes both buses before the reset providers
bind. With this change the same deferred-reset condition occurs, both
controller probes finish, and all four codecs bind and produce audio.

--- a/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
@@ -1996,13 +1996,13 @@
 					qcom_swrm_all_slaves_online(ctrl),
 					msecs_to_jiffies(TIMEOUT_MS))) {
 			qcom_swrm_log_boot_slaves(ctrl);
-			dev_err(dev, "boot enumeration failed: slaves still missing\n");
-			ret = -ETIMEDOUT;
-			goto err_master_add;
+			/* Reset suppliers may be queued behind this probe on the same worker. */
+			dev_info(dev, "boot enumeration pending: allowing deferred codec probes\n");
 		}
 	}
 	qcom_swrm_log_boot_slaves(ctrl);
-	dev_info(dev, "boot enumeration complete: all slaves attached\n");
+	if (qcom_swrm_all_slaves_online(ctrl))
+		dev_info(dev, "boot enumeration complete: all slaves attached\n");
 	ret = qcom_swrm_register_dais(ctrl);
 	if (ret)
 		goto err_master_add;
